        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.083,
            0.743,
            0.125
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Discuss with your friends and make a list of at least five products that we get from forests."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.15,
            0.745,
            0.354
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Forests are a natural home for many wild animals, including birds and insects. Forests provide food and shelter to them. In nature, every animal depends on other life forms for survival. The diversity of life forms ensures food for every living being. However, over the years, the forest cover has been decreasing, mainly due to human activities like large scale cutting of trees. It takes many years to grow a new forest or restore lost forests. Therefore, we must preserve and use forests responsibly so that they get enough time to regenerate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.355,
            0.443,
            0.581
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Van Mahotsav is a weeklong event celebrated across the country during the month of July. It is a forest festival during which new plants and trees are planted, and awareness about respecting forests is raised. The aim of the event is to increase the green cover. You too can plan a Van Mahotsav in your community."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.493,
            0.37,
            0.832,
            0.518
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What are the consequences of cutting a large forest area? Make a presentation or do a role play, or write a story or a poem that",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " shows what could happen if we continue to cut down ? "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "trees in our forests.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.622,
            0.566,
            0.762
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "From ancient times, India had a tradition of respecting, protecting and preserving forests. You have already learnt about sacred groves in the chapter ‘Diversity in the Living World’. Many efforts have been made by common people to prevent the cutting of trees, and"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.58,
            0.624,
            0.831,
            0.793
          ],
          "content": [
            {
